  "detailed_description": "The Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana: Establishment of Medium RAS / Biofloc Culture System,  introduced by the Ministry Of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry &amp; Dairying, Government of India, aims to provide capital assistance to fish farmers and entrepreneurs for establishing medium-scale Recirculatory Aquaculture Systems (RAS) and Biofloc systems. These models promote high-density fish production in controlled environments, significantly reducing land and water usage. It is a centrally funded scheme with a 50:50 cost-sharing pattern between the Central and State Governments.\n\n- For RAS: Minimum 6 tanks of 30 m³ each (10 tons/crop)- For Biofloc: 25 tanks of 4 m diameter and 1 m height\n",
  "eligibility": "\n1. The applicant must be a permanent resident of Haryana and possess a valid Parivar Pehchan Patra (PPP).\n1. The applicant must have access to own land or hold a registered lease for a minimum period of 10 years.\n1. The applicant must ensure that the land is free from any legal and financial encumbrances.\n1. The applicant must have access to a reliable water source such as a canal, tube well, river, or similar.\n1. The applicant must provide a valid training certificate in fisheries or aquaculture.\n1. The applicant must agree to manage and maintain the system at their own cost after setup.\n1. The applicant must submit a Detailed Project Report (DPR) or a Self-Contained Proposal (SCP).\n1. The applicant must sign an agreement with the Department of Fisheries to avail benefits under the scheme.\n\n",
  "exclusions": "<br>\n\n",
